Unwind every patch already installed when `instrument()` fails part-way through,
which it does against an SDK that renames or relocates one of the wrapped
methods. `instrument()` marks the instrumentor as instrumented only once
patching has finished, so the wrappers that did install were stranded —
`uninstrument()` declined as already uninstrumented — while a retry was let
through and wrapped the wrapper. Measured against a relocated
`receive_messages`, one `query()` call then produced two `invoke_agent` spans in
two separate traces.
